{
  "id": 217778344,
  "iid": 10321,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "MC-NMF: set TCP/9389 (ADWS) as default port",
  "description": "2 years ago, @uhei introduced support for ADWS dissection with https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/16861\n\nHowever, it isn't enabled by default for ADWS traffic on port 9389. Users have to know about this, and configure \"Decode as...\" with MC-NMF for this port (as I described in https://clement.notin.org/blog/2020/11/16/ntlm-relay-of-adws-connections-with-impacket/#wcf--nettcp-binding). It's a bit annoying and it makes it less likely that folks will benefit from this great work :disappointed: \n\nSo I suggest to do this automatically :smile: \n\n[MC-NMF] does not have a defined port https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/mc-nmf/51b5eb53-f488-4b74-b21d-8a498f016b61\nbut 9389 is ADWS port https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-adcap/cfff3d7f-e7cd-4529-86a0-4de89efe3855\nwhich relies on [MC-NMF], so by doing this, all ADWS traffic on port 9389 is properly dissected by default\n\n- before, no dissection of ADWS:\n![image](/uploads/e03883c07d2911084f1c31312378579a/image.png)\n\n- after, dissection works without configuring any custom \"Decode as...\"!\n![image](/uploads/88b9a474b8737a2e36a2c2b98f32e32e/image.png)\n\nSample pcap is available on: https://wiki.wireshark.org/SampleCaptures#adws",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-04-14T21:43:15.527Z",
